  "label": "Tumble Hill",
  "about": "A named place: the open south-west-facing apron below the north wall, about 500 m from the tree village: a level ledge at 150 m, then about 260 m of fall line at a mean grade near 0.38 and never steeper than 0.54, down to the meadow. Re-surveyed on 2026-11-07 for the grown valley, whose walls are too steep and whose high ground is snow from top to bottom; the old site became a cliff. The props keep their places along and across the fall line; the three snow piles are pine cones, since no snow lies this low in late spring. Its props are core-owned because the place has a name (AGENTS.md); they are toys for the reaction table, not plantings, and nothing about them is persisted. The placement keeps trees off `fall_line_xy_m`.",
